# React Native Architecture Guidelines

## Core Principles

- Use a feature-oriented architecture rather than organizing the entire application by technical type.
- Keep business logic separate from UI components.
- Keep components small, focused, and reusable.
- Prefer composition over inheritance.
- Follow existing project conventions before introducing a new architectural pattern.
- Do not introduce abstractions unless they solve a real problem.
- Avoid over-engineering simple features.
- Keep dependencies flowing in one direction: UI → application/feature logic → data/infrastructure.
- Business logic should not depend directly on React Native UI components.
- Avoid circular dependencies.
- Always double check the features if it follows the stated plans.

